# A CONTROL program that uses DATA blocks as totality oracles. Run with:
#   python -m jtv.cli examples/oracle.jtv --mode control
#
# `i < n`, `sum plus i`, and `i plus 1` are all DATA expressions: each one
# is guaranteed to halt the instant it's checked/evaluated (it's addition
# and comparison over finite terms — nothing to loop on). The `while` loop
# itself is CONTROL, openly Turing-complete: nothing in JtV proves this
# particular loop terminates. It happens to, because `i` counts up to a
# fixed `n`, but that is ordinary reasoning about this program, not a
# guarantee the language gives you. See README LIMITATIONS.
begin
  n = 5
  sum = 0
  i = 0
  while i < n do
    begin
      sum = sum plus i
      i = i plus 1
    end
  print(sum)
end
